======================================================================
   k = 1: coeff(s^1) = k * Wronskian(C_k)  -> True
   k = 2: coeff(s^3) = k * Wronskian(C_k)  -> True
   k = 3: coeff(s^5) = k * Wronskian(C_k)  -> True
   k = 4: coeff(s^7) = k * Wronskian(C_k)  -> True
   k = 5: coeff(s^9) = k * Wronskian(C_k)  -> True
  [PASS] the top coefficient is k*Wronskian(C_k) for k = 1..5
